WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.402
[...]

00:00:04.402 --> 00:00:07.613
Consider two dilemmas.

00:00:07.613 --> 00:00:10.777
You are a university
student, and you discover

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:17.372
that your roommate, who is also your
best friend, has cheated on an exam.

00:00:17.372 --> 00:00:22.707
You wonder whether to report
her to university authorities.

00:00:22.707 --> 00:00:25.919
Or suppose you are an
excellent swimmer and you're

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:30.184
a member of your country's
Olympic swimming team.

00:00:30.184 --> 00:00:32.968
Shortly before the
swimming event you discover

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:38.848
that a teammate has been taking
illegal performance-enhancing drugs.

00:00:38.848 --> 00:00:43.129
You wonder whether to report
him to the authorities.

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:46.614
Thinking about these
dilemmas raises a question

00:00:46.614 --> 00:00:50.020
about loyalty and truth-telling.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:54.608
Do you think it is sometimes
right to lie or to hide the truth

00:00:54.608 --> 00:01:00.038
to protect a friend, a teammate, or a
compatriot who's done something wrong?

